  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In facial isomer, three&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;atoms present on one face of the octahedron. Similarly, three ammonia molecules are present on one face of the octahedron. All 3 same ligands have&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;bond angle between them.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/db1cc5fd-819d-4f45-9e7e-2685a8609c8a-9896015.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 344px;\" /></p><p>The&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cl</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Co</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>Cl</mi></math>&nbsp;bond angle in above octahedral complex is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math></p>",
